.TH 3DMOUSED 8 2026-11-10 "3dmouse-linux 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
3dmoused \- 3DMouse Linux device broker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 3dmoused
.RB [ \-\-mode " auto|native-owner|integrated-spacenav|passive-monitor" ]
.RB [ \-\-input " auto|hidraw|evdev" ]
.RB [ \-\-uinput " PATH|none" ]
.RB [ \-\-spnav\-socket " PATH" ]
.RB [ \-\-control\-socket " PATH" ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 3dmoused
discovers 3Dconnexion 6-DOF devices, decodes their HID reports, and applies the axis pipeline of
the active profile.
It serves the libspnav-compatible socket that native applications such as Blender, FreeCAD and
OpenSCAD use, and owns a uinput virtual keyboard and mouse for desktop actions requested by
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1).
It normally runs as the systemd unit
.IR 3dmoused.service ,
as root with no capabilities and a restricted device allowlist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode
.B auto
(the default) yields to an already running libspnav server such as spacenavd
.RB ( integrated-spacenav ),
and otherwise owns the devices
.RB ( native-owner ).
.B passive-monitor
only reports status.
spacenavd is never stopped or disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-input
Device access path. hidraw is preferred, with evdev as the fallback.
.TP
.B \-\-uinput
The virtual input device, or
.B none
to disable injection.
.TP
.BR \-\-spnav\-socket " (default " /run/spnav.sock )
.TP
.BR \-\-control\-socket " (default " /run/3dmouse/broker.sock )
Control clients are authorised by SO_PEERCRED: root, the active seat user, or the service's own
uid.
.SH FILES
.I /run/spnav.sock
.br
.I /run/3dmouse/broker.sock
.br
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-3dmouse-linux.rules
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 3dmousectl (1),
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1),
.BR 3dmouse-config (1),
.BR spacenavd (8)
